rows=[
(1,'KEEP',[X],'theory','Inferring unusual rainbow rays from supplied zenith/horizon observations','Full narrative provides angular width, dawn/dusk geometry and comparative brightness. Refraction, internal reflection and stationary ray deflection constrain a suitable droplet-index model and companion rainbow. Alien travel and chemical identity are context, not specialized physics prerequisites.'),
(2,'KEEP',[I],'theory','Inverse central force for Galileo circular fall paths','Actual historical orbit drawing and launch constraints were inspected. Newtonian angular momentum/Binet geometry derive which central force generates circles through the centre and test consistency across tower latitude/height.'),
(3,'KEEP',[X],'numerical','Daylight and twilight duration across latitudes and seasons','Spherical Earth, illuminated hemisphere, fixed twilight depression and declination interval are explicitly supplied. Spherical trigonometry and extrema/calculus give durations including polar cases; no atmosphere model is required.'),
(4,'KEEP',[I],'numerical','Leaning motorcycle friction and detached-wheel trajectory','Steady centripetal force/torque determine minimum friction. Rigid rolling-wheel dynamics and angular momentum predict the separated wheel path under declared realistic mass/inertia/speed values.'),
(5,'KEEP',[I],'numerical','Planet motion under a fully supplied time-varying Newton constant','G(t)=G0*t0/t is explicitly printed and the task retains Newton gravity. Ordinary central-force ODEs/angular momentum describe evolving orbits; the Dirac reference is context and no relativistic cosmology is needed.'),
(6,'KEEP',[I,II],'theory','Release of a string stretched by its own weight','Ordinary axial Hooke elasticity, initial gravity tension and longitudinal wave propagation give release dynamics under a declared elastic-string idealization. No flexural/3D tensor model is centrally requested.'),
(7,'KEEP',[I,II],'theory','Increasing rocking frequency while oscillation amplitude damps','Rigid rolling/rocking geometry can give an amplitude-dependent period. Damping energy reduces amplitude and may shorten the period; ordinary nonlinear oscillation quadrature suffices.'),
(8,'KEEP',[I,VI],'numerical','Classical scattering from a charged wire near a grounded sheet','Explicit wire/electrode/potential/beam geometry defines ordinary electrostatics and Newton charged-particle motion. Impact-parameter/angular mapping yields the two-dimensional differential cross section without a quantum Rutherford rule.'),
(9,'REJECT',[],'theory','Relativistic correction to Rutherford scattering','The central potential is printed but relativistic energy-momentum/velocity relation and trajectory dynamics are not. Those unsupplied laws centrally determine the requested cross section.'),
(10,'KEEP',[I],'theory','Small elastic indentation correction to rigid-sphere scattering','The source explicitly idealizes high linear spring stiffness and shallow indentation. Newtonian central contact-force trajectory and impact-parameter geometry yield differential/total cross sections and the hard-wall limit without a microscopic contact model.'),
(11,'KEEP',[I],'numerical','Oil-density gravitational anomaly and a fully defined potential Hessian','The cylindrical density-replacement model and exact Hessian definition are provided. Newton potential integration and second derivatives determine gravity/gradient estimates and pendulum detectability. Tensor notation is supplied calculus, not GR or elastic stress machinery.'),
(12,'KEEP',[I],'theory','Gravitational separation of two halves of a stipulated egg-shaped asteroid','Homogeneous hemisphere/half-ellipsoid geometry and small deformation are supplied, and cohesion is explicitly cut away. Newton mutual potential/force integration and a perturbative expansion compare axial/transverse displacements.'),
(13,'KEEP',[I,II],'theory','Effective cart drag from a fully specified continuum of pendulum oscillators','Point penduli coupled through cart motion and the explicit spectral-density definition determine oscillator response and the reaction force. Eliminating ordinary Newton oscillator coordinates and averaging the given constant density is integral mathematics, not a required stochastic bath theory.'),
(14,'REJECT',[],'numerical','Dynamic recoil and performance of an unmodelled composite reflex bow','Historical materials/shape are described but flexural moment-curvature law, composite limb energy and moving-limb/string coupling are not supplied. These unsupplied beam/material dynamics centrally determine arrow acceleration/speed and the design comparisons.'),
(15,'BORDERLINE',[I,II],'theory','Constructing a model for flow-excited periodic tree-branch motion','The statement permits model construction, so a coarse spring/drag/buoyancy feedback model may stay in ordinary physics. A quantitatively faithful flexible-branch/fluid instability instead needs unsupplied beam/vortex or flow coupling. No intended model level is given; preserve the whole-task ambiguity.'),
(16,'KEEP',[I,II],'numerical','Tidal synchronization in a explicitly proposed damped two-mass model','The source replaces the Moon with two point masses and a damped spring. Newtonian tidal force, internal spring extension/lag and angular momentum/energy exchange test synchronization without unsupplied continuum tidal rheology.'),
(17,'KEEP',[I],'theory','Long-range capillary attraction of floating coins','Surface tension/curvature pressure and hydrostatic restoring pressure define meniscus deformation and interaction. Linear far-field geometry/Bessel mathematics or the permitted lower-dimensional analogue gives force dependence without specialized fluid dynamics.'),
(18,'KEEP',[I,II],'theory','Power needed for waves of a specified typical height','Ordinary gravity-wave energy, energy conservation and loss/flux rates give a parametric estimate. Area/height alone do not determine a unique stationary power without frequency/damping or buildup time; that source insufficiency can be demonstrated with allowed physics rather than adding turbulence theory.'),
(19,'KEEP',[I,VI,VII],'numerical','Classical charge redistribution and magnetic field of a rotating conductor','A classical free-carrier force balance combines rotation, electrostatic equilibrium and charge neutrality; rotating induced charge gives Biot-Savart fields. Earth-field feasibility is an ordinary magnitude comparison. No microscopic band or quantum spin theory is demanded.'),
(20,'KEEP',[IV,V],'theory','Opposite liquid-level thermal changes in closed saturated-vapor vessels','Mass/volume conservation, liquid expansion and vapor saturation variation explain opposite level slopes for different fill fractions. Ordinary phase equilibrium/Clausius-Clapeyron scaling yields a balance condition; no chemistry model is required.'),
(21,'KEEP',[],'data_analysis','Trend-fit variance under explicitly supplied independent Gaussian noise','The least-squares estimator, zero-trend independent annual model, sigma and N are supplied. Estimator covariance gives RMS fitted slope for both N values. Climate-system dynamics is not required by this stipulated statistical task.'),
(22,'REJECT',[],'theory','Elastic interaction energy of supplied point-defect displacement fields','The displacement field is provided, but strain/stress constitutive tensor, elastic-energy functional and defect coupling are not. Those unsupplied continuum-elastic laws are needed to infer interaction energy rather than just differentiate a displacement.'),
(23,'REJECT',[],'theory','Centre of mass and lifting of relativistically rolling wheels','No Lorentz transformation, energy-weighted centre or relativistic stress/work accounting is supplied. These central unsupplied relativistic solid mechanics rules determine both requested results.'),
(24,'REJECT',[],'theory','Generalized inertial tensor for a partially supplied energy-momentum function','E=f(p), Z(E), F=p-dot and a=v-dot are provided, but the canonical energy-gradient velocity rule linking p to v is not. The Hamilton/Lagrange hint names that missing dynamical formalism, central to every mass expression. Preserve the established arbitrary-Hamiltonian boundary.'),
(25,'KEEP',[VI],'theory','Circuit survival under fully supplied stochastic burnout laws','Both forty-bulb circuit topologies and constant/power-proportional Poisson hazard rules are stated and diagrammed. Ohm/Kirchhoff power updates and exponential/order statistics give burnout/open-circuit times under a declared source-voltage/resistance convention.'),
(26,'REJECT',[],'theory','Minimum-uncertainty quantum eigenstate and oscillator identification','Neither quantum position/momentum operators, uncertainty inequality/saturation states nor eigen-equation are supplied. These central specialized quantum laws are required; an arbitrary Hamiltonian also needs an unstated conventional kinetic-plus-local-potential restriction for the claimed theorem.'),
(27,'REJECT',[],'theory','Symmetry constraints on a spin-dependent quantum scattering matrix','Asymptotic scattering wave and matrix are supplied, but spin time-reversal/rotation representations and scattering-state symmetry actions are not. Those central quantum spin rules define both requested constraints.'),
(28,'KEEP',[XII],'data_analysis','Half-life uncertainty from five explicitly supplied nuclear lifetimes','All five measured times, precision and confidence level are printed. Ordinary exponential nuclear decay and finite-sample Gamma/order-statistical estimation determine rate/half-life sampling distribution and confidence bounds; no superheavy production theory is needed.'),
(29,'KEEP',[XII],'numerical','Alpha activity after filtering daughters from a supplied radon chain','Initial secular equilibrium, complete filtration, constant small airflow, chain and all half-lives are supplied. Linear production/decay equations through collection and after shutdown yield alpha intensity and plot. No detector microphysics or external decay scheme is necessary under the stated idealization.'),
(30,'REJECT',[],'theory','Quantum spin decoherence under an unspecified noisy-field master model','White-noise field is described, but quantum spin Hamiltonian, density-matrix evolution and state/coherence rules are not supplied. Ito mathematics alone does not provide that missing quantum dynamics.'),
(31,'REJECT',[],'theory','Arbitrary-spin Heisenberg position dynamics and projections','Formal Hamiltonian/spin labels do not supply commutators, spin-matrix action, Heisenberg evolution or expectation/projection interpretation. Those central quantum rules control all three requests.'),
(32,'REJECT',[],'theory','Relativistic invariant-mass endpoints in a particle decay cascade','Decay chain, selection thresholds and a four-momentum invariant expression are supplied, but four-vector mass shell/rest-frame/boost kinematics and individual mass inputs are not operationally provided. Those central unsupplied relativistic tools determine the endpoints; exotic particle names are not the reason.'),
(33,'KEEP',[I],'numerical','Vehicles and effective terrain on a stipulated rigid rotating meridian ring','Entire pp7-8 story supplies an unbreakable Earth-fixed meridian ring. Newtonian gravity/centrifugal potential, constrained motion and Coriolis/contact force give terrain, free/engine-driven paths and tire demands under chosen vehicle data. Structural material modelling is explicitly idealized away.')]
