notes={1:'Droplet index/shape is an inferred ray-optics model; statement does not supply a unique chemical composition. Do not invent spectroscopic identification.',4:'Actual minimum-friction question includes rider lean 60 degrees. Detached-wheel mass/inertia and launch state need chosen realistic values; author credit continues p3.',5:'Exact G(t)=G0*t0/t is supplied. The 1938 article is not necessary to supply the law and was not acquired as unrelated cosmology.',6:'Linear axial Hooke-string idealization and mass/stiffness parameters must be declared; inextensible fall is a distinct limiting model.',10:'Very high string rate is interpreted as local linear indentation stiffness as stated; do not replace it with unprovided Hertz contact physics.',11:'Oil must replace denser host material; density contrast rather than added positive mass controls the gravity anomaly. Hessian is explicitly defined.',13:'Rendered K(omega)=sum_alpha (pi/2)*m_alpha*omega_alpha^2*delta(omega-omega_alpha). Continuum support/cutoff and distribution-limit conventions must be declared.',14:'No bow load-deflection curve or flexural/composite limb model is supplied. Historical dimensions alone do not provide arrow acceleration.',15:'Model level not specified. An ordinary lumped oscillator with immersion/drag feedback is permitted in principle, but actual instability mechanism is not established.',16:'Two-point-mass damped spring is explicitly proposed; spring/damping constants and orbit parameters may be selected/retained, not a realistic lunar rheology assertion.',18:'S and h fix an energy scale, not a unique power. Buildup duration, loss/escape rate and wavelength/statistical wave-height convention are missing.',19:'Classical free-electron/carrier approximation must be stated; this is not a quantitative semiconductor/metal band model or Earth dynamo explanation.',22:'Given displacement field is acknowledged; it does not supply the stress/elastic-energy relation needed for interaction.',24:'Both F=p-dot and a=v-dot are actually provided; missing rule is specifically velocity versus the arbitrary supplied energy-momentum function.',25:'Supply type/amplitude and bulb resistance versus heating are not fixed; use a declared ideal fixed-voltage/resistance model and note current-source alternative.',26:'The theorem is not true for arbitrary Hamiltonians sharing an oscillator eigenstate; a conventional local potential plus quadratic kinetic term would have to be specified.',27:'An asymptotic matrix is defined, but spin symmetry representations are not. Do not confuse partial model with a complete quantum law.',28:'Use non-Gaussian finite-sample lifetime/rate statistics and a stated confidence-interval convention; no false high precision from five events.',29:'Actual printed 214Po half-life is 64 microseconds; preserve provided value in this exercise. Pure single-branch chain and secular collection approximation are source assumptions.',32:'m^2=(sum four-momenta)^2 is printed; endpoint numbers and intermediate masses are not a full operational relativistic cascade model.',33:'Source expressly says material can withstand everything; structural nanotube physics is not asked. Engine-driven speed/time is parametric without an engine-force law.'}
